#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""CinterForgeTerminal: documented entry point for developers and builders.

This script is the *single user-facing command driver* for the Terminal repo.
Use ``./Cinter <command>`` on macOS/Linux or ``Cinter.cmd`` on Windows.

PUBLIC INTERFACES
    setup / build / stage / test / all   — application lifecycle
    host                                 — C++ Host lifecycle / diagnostics
    clone / fork                         — maintained source management
    pull / publish / fetch / verify      — explicitly scoped R2 transfers
    status / toolchain / install         — read-only diagnostics or SDK install

BUILD SAFETY
    Setup prepares pinned dependencies and runs real Bedrock acceptance.
    Build produces the three native apps and unified optional DevTools ZIP.
    Stage installs and checks archives; ``all all`` never publishes.
    Child build tools, not this CLI, own their detailed platform implementations.
    Only the lifecycle that started managed VMs may stop them.
    Every lifecycle invocation produces persistent Build/Stage/Setup/Test logs
    and PASS/FAIL summaries, not console-only output.

DIRECTORY OWNERSHIP
    ``build/`` is authored source (bootstrap/resource inputs).
    ``webapp/`` is authored browser and Python application source.
    The *sibling* ``Builds/`` is the sole generated-artifact/cache directory,
    unless a documented runtime belongs in the designated steamapps tree.

Internal helpers are below the public dispatcher and grouped by purpose.
Source-management code was moved here from ``build/fork.py``; it never resets
an existing checkout. A separate ``CPH`` user-facing script is not required.
"""
